    "source": "duboce-triangle-context-statement",
    "style": "Mission Revival",
    "note": "By far the best of only four Mission Revival buildings the statement finds in Duboce Triangle, and one of the six religious and fraternal buildings in the survey area. The congregation, a Disciples of Christ church that came from the South of Market area after the 1906 earthquake, still owns and operates it. One of the properties the statement puts forward as a potential city landmark candidate, a list it calls 37 properties in one passage and 38 in another and prints with 38 entries; it says further research will be required to confirm any of them. Christopher VerPlanck's context statement of 2022 surveyed 552 properties in Duboce Triangle for the Duboce Triangle Neighborhood Association."
